.claude/.pr*
.clone/
.superpowers/
skills-lock.json
test-results/
.pipeline-state/

# Skill symlinks/junctions managed by Claude Code tooling point into .agents/
# and break git-bash dir walks on Windows (MSYS2 opendir returns ENOSYS for
# NTFS junctions, triggering "Function not implemented" warnings that then
# corrupt lint-staged via tinyexec's merged stderr). Ignore the whole dir,
# then allow-list the real tracked skills. New tracked skills need a new
# allow-list line here.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/changelog/
!.claude/skills/dev-server/
!.claude/skills/e2e/
!.claude/skills/e2e-debug/
!.claude/skills/release/
!.claude/skills/screenshots/

# Developer-local Claude project memory (per its own header: "Gitignored.
# Local-only context"). Was accidentally committed in 76949f8; untracked in
# the documentation audit.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Generated design-baseline gallery (`npm run capture:design-baselines`).
# Generated on demand, never committed — see docs/design-system-impl/baseline-procedure.md.
# It was committed until #1190: a 3.1MB non-diffable file that embeds today's date at
# capture time, so every regeneration dirtied it even when nothing had visually changed.
docs/design-system-impl/preview/baselines/baselines.html

# Generated v1.0 performance-gate fixture (`node scripts/fixtures/make-perf-doc.mjs`).
# ~200KB of seeded lorem plus its annotation seed — reproducible from the checked-in
# generator, so the artifact itself is noise in the history. The GENERATOR is tracked;
# this output is not. See docs/roadmap.md §"Performance gate".
tests/perf/.generated/

# WhatsApp MCP (piwapp) session artifacts. These are LIVE CREDENTIALS -- the JSON
# holds noise_key, signed_identity_key, signed_pre_key and adv_secret_key, and the
# sibling .keys file is the encrypted keystore. The server writes them into
# whatever directory it was started from, which for an MCP server configured at
# user level is the repo you happen to be working in. Untracked-but-committable is
# the dangerous state: one `git add -A` publishes a working WhatsApp session.
# Ignored rather than deleted -- removing them unpairs the device.
piwapp_auth.json
piwapp_auth.json.keys
piwapp_qr.png

# Python bytecode from the spike harnesses under scripts/spikes/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Codex CLI scratch output. Untracked today only because all four files in it
# happen to end in `.log` (the `*.log` rule above) -- the first non-log file
# written there would become a commit candidate, which is why this repo's plan
# documents carried a manual "do not commit .codex files" reminder. Nothing in
# the repo reads this directory. Blanket by choice: if a project-level Codex
# config is ever worth tracking, add an explicit `!.codex/<file>` line here,
# the way `.claude/skills/*` does above.
#
# `.codex/*`, NOT `.codex/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so under the directory form the `!` line above would
# silently do nothing -- `git status` stays clean and the file looks tracked
# when it is not. The content glob is what makes the escape hatch real, and it
# is why the `.claude/skills/*` precedent is written that way too.
.codex/*
